turboexl3_ling vendors third-party code below. Each copy is unchanged but for the edits scripts/sync-mlx-serve.sh makes,
listed at its top (among them, the copies' blank lines are taken out), and those in patches/*.patch. It builds
against the mlx-serve plugin kit and turboexl3 (build.zig.zon, by URL and hash).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mlx-serve
https://github.com/ddalcu/mlx-serve
Copyright (c) 2026 David Dalcu
Licensed under the MIT License.

src/mlx_serve/ (generated by scripts/prepare.sh, not committed) holds the files of mlx-serve's src/ this plugin compiles,
at their mlx-serve paths, from the commit in this plugin's MLX_SERVE_REF: the slices scripts/slice.txt (the Ling model,
plugins/bailing_hybrid, and what it imports: plugins/glm5_next's trunk, KDA and config readers, the sdk blocks) and
scripts/slice-stream.txt (the expert streamer) name, with the Metal kernels and other files they embed, and the read
pool's C (sdk/weights/streamed/csrc/q3_lookahead4_exl3.c, q3_lookahead4.h). overlay/mlx_serve/ is copied over it: the
files in the script's EDGES list, which are this plugin's own code at mlx-serve paths, not copies (mlx/kernels.zig,
sdk/weights/streamed/ling_source.zig, sdk/quant/exl3/format.zig). patches/*.patch then edit the copies, one patch an
area: ling-trunk.patch (the trunk's EXL3 projections, the MoE block, the layer-major prompt pass and the shared sdk
utilities' exported names), ling-kda.patch (the KDA mixer), ling-mla.patch (the MLA attention) and ling-stream.patch
(the expert streamer); the patches are this plugin's.

src/host_shims.zig stands in for mlx-serve's sdk/weights/streamed/csrc/mlx_event_shim.cpp, mlx_alloc_shim.cpp,
mlx_launch_cache.inc and q3_event_shim.mm (their C symbols, over the server's host table); it is this plugin's code,
taken from CommunityServe/plugins' turboexl3_ds41.

